METHOD NOTE (docs-gate-engineer's two false-negative traps, both avoided here)
  · the resolver reads the FILESYSTEM (`existsSync`), never the git index — a wave ADDS files that
    are still untracked (`??`) until the captain's commit, so a `git ls-files`/`git show`-based
    resolver would report every newly added script MISSING and produce a false negative for exactly
    the wave being audited. Re-measure AFTER the commit to see the same set.
  · bare basenames in prose are NOT tokens: the manual writes QA lanes as
    `skills/dsh-qa/scripts/<case>.mjs`, so a naive `scripts/*.mjs` scan invents ghosts
    (bundle-lifecycle, preset-conformance, preset-register, lib/session-evidence,
    lib/workspace-isolation). This audit matches full path tokens and resolves each with an explicit
    prefix rule (as written, else `skills/dsh-qa/scripts/<basename>`, else `scripts/<basename>`).
